// 1. Build features: max prob, margin, entropy, $p^2$, $\text{margin}^2$, $\text{entropy}\cdot\text{conf}$, $p(1-p)$, group one-hots, first 10 cols of X.
// 2. Train GBM (n_est=150, depth=3, lr=0.1) to predict correctness; raw_scores = predict_proba.
// 3. global_thr = quantile$_{1-c}$(raw_scores); per_group_thr$_g$ = quantile$_{1-c}$(raw_scores$|$group=g).
// 4. Sweep $\alpha\in\{0,0.02,\dots,1\}$, set thr$_g=\alpha\cdot$per_group$_g+(1-\alpha)\cdot$global; keep candidate if coverage $\in[c-0.025, c+0.025]$.
// 5. Score candidates by $0.4\cdot\text{sel\_risk}+0.3\cdot\text{worst\_group\_risk}+0.6\cdot\text{def\_gap}+2\cdot|\text{cov}-c|$, take min.
// 6. Local search: ±0.03 offsets per group around the best blend, re-evaluate same objective.
// 7. accept = scores ≥ per-group thr.

// 1. Train balanced logistic regression on confidence+group+X features → meta scores.
// 2. Initial per-group thresholds = quantile$_{1-c}$(scores$|$g).
// 3. Loop ≤15 times with step $\Delta=0.005$:
//    - compute per-group deferral; if cov drift $>0.04$ or gap $<0.01$ stop.
//    - identify high-deferral group $g_+$ and low-deferral $g_-$.
//    - lower thr$_{g_+}$ by Δ (clip 0.01), raise thr$_{g_-}$ by Δ (clip 0.99).
//    - keep update if cov within ±tol; else single-side adjustment.
//    - track best seen by deferral-gap.
// 4. accept if meta_score ≥ thr$_{g(x)}$.

// 1. Build features (confidence stats + group one-hots up to 10 + raw X) and inverse-frequency sample weights.
// 2. Fit GBC (n_est=100, depth=3, lr=0.05) with sample_weight; get OOF correctness probs via 5-fold cross_val_predict.
// 3. global_thr = quantile$_{1-c}$(OOF scores); per-group cov_g = mean(OOF$|$g ≥ global_thr).
// 4. Sweep $\lambda\in[0,1]$ in 51 steps: target cov$_g$ = $\lambda c + (1-\lambda)\,\text{cov}_g$; thr$_g$ = quantile$_{1-\text{target}}$(OOF$|$g).
// 5. Compute accept; objective = $\text{worst\_group\_risk}+5\,\text{def\_gap}+0.5\,\text{overall\_risk}$; pick min.
// 6. accept = OOF score ≥ thr$_{g(x)}$.

// 1. Train LR (balanced) and GB (n_est=100, depth=2, lr=0.1) on confidence features → cal_scores = $\tfrac{1}{2}(\hat p_{LR}+\hat p_{GB})$.
// 2. global_thr = quantile$_{1-c}$(cal_scores).
// 3. For each group g: per_group_thr$_g$ = quantile$_{1-c}$(cal_scores$|$g); $\lambda_g=\min(n_g/n,0.5)$; thr$_g=\lambda_g$ per_group$_g+(1-\lambda_g)$ global.
